    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **68 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field per the spec. The project exposes derived owner attributes as `@Transient` read-time getters on the `Owner` model, which MapStruct auto-maps into the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` \u2014 no controller or new pipeline function needed.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getOwnerSegment()`:\n   ```java\n   @Transient\n   public String getOwnerSegment() {\n       String tier = getMembershipLevel() >= 3 ? \"PREMIUM\" : \"STANDARD\";\n       String area = REGION_TIMEZONE.containsKey(getLocality()) ? \"METRO\" : \"REGIONAL\";\n       return tier + \"_\" + area;\n   }\n   ```\n   It reuses the existing `getMembershipLevel()` (TIER: `PREMIUM` at level \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`) and `getLocality()` (AREA: `METRO` when the locality is a known region \u2014 NSW/VIC/QLD, which are exactly the keys of the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` map \u2014 else `REGIONAL`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` schema property (string, readOnly) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\nBoth `Cp55Tests` cases pass (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one), and the full suite of 68 tests stays green.",
